## 5. What the oracle is, and what could not be run
The official MCP Python SDK (mcp 2.3.0, mcp-types 2.3.0) was downloaded from PyPI into the scratch folder and
read, not run: installing it into a scratch venv was refused by this environment's auto-mode check as code
from outside. The test client's rules are taken from its source: mcp_types/_v2025_11_25/__init__.py (generated
from schema/2025-11-25.json, sha256 4e01628360a2149892eab8f298ceee626d24a58862184eb8ec85d95b8f353e31 per its
header), mcp/client/_probe.py (server/discover first, any error -> initialize), mcp/client/session.py
(initialize refuses a version outside 2024-11-05 .. 2025-11-25). The spec site modelcontextprotocol.io could
not be resolved from here. No MCP app (Claude Desktop, LM Studio, ...) was connected; the JSON entry in
novacore/README.md is UNVERIFIED. msvcrt locking on Windows is UNVERIFIED (no Windows host).
