## 6. A test that was wrong, corrected before the first commit (AGENTS.md rule 7: which, and why)
The first run of novacore/tests/test_mcp.py failed in test_a_client_session_as_the_official_sdk_runs_it:
it expected the call refused on its argument rules (apps_open with app "calculator", not a listed app)
to appear in mcp-events.jsonl as applied=False. The broker logs only runs: its argument check returns
"denied" before anything runs or is recorded (novacore/src/novacore/capabilities.py, _run_desktop;
novacore/SCOPE.md: "logs every run in the chained outbox"). The test was wrong, not the server. It now
expects two events and says why. Consequence worth knowing: an MCP app probing tools with bad arguments
leaves no outbox trace; only its runs do.

